Package: silhouetteTree
Title: Silhouette-Based Choice of Cluster Number and Cluster-Coloured Trees, with a Point-and-Click App
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Tomoyoshi", "Kaneko", email = "kanekotomoyoshi@akane.waseda.jp", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Chooses the number of clusters by the mean silhouette width and
    draws dendrograms or phylogenies coloured by cluster. Input is either a
    Newick tree (distances are patristic, via ape::cophenetic.phylo) or a table
    of measurements with numeric, binary and categorical columns (Gower
    distance via cluster::daisy, so that large absolute values of one column do
    not dominate; Euclidean and Manhattan with min-max or z-score
    normalisation are also available). Follows the analysis of Kaneko et al.
    (2025) <doi:10.1128/jvi.01061-25>. A Shiny application (run_app()) makes the
    whole workflow available without writing code.
